 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-FeatureDefinition">Feature Definition=
</h1>
    <p><span class=3D"jira-issue" data-jira-key=3D"NWPI-6182" data-client-i=
d=3D"SINGLE_6770dc6c-0646-39a6-a1ea-561a14a12e2f_1393941690_8ab247629ffb6d5=
c01a0066f1fcb0034"> <a href=3D"https://jira.bnc.ca/browse/NWPI-6182" class=
=3D"jira-issue-key"><span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-wait issue-placeholder=
"></span>NWPI-6182</a> - <span class=3D"summary">Getting issue details...</=
span> <span class=3D"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-default iss=
ue-placeholder">STATUS</span> </span></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h3 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-UserGoals">User Goals</h3>
    <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">The overarching goal of this =
feature is<span> to optimize the level of controls in the access control so=
lution and the product feature hierarchy<strong><em> </em></strong>so that =
Platform users would be configured to access the data &amp; actions of prod=
uct features according to their access right</span><span>.&nbsp;</span></sp=
an></p>
    <ul>
     <li>NBIN Product team would like to have the ability to=20
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"><strong>Manage product fe=
ature hierarchy: </strong>Reorganize or expand the products easily so that =
the access control can be targeted to the specific feature level or feature=
 configuration</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"><strong>Manage firm featu=
re packages: </strong>Bundle a group of product features and configurations=
 in a "digital package" in order to facilitate firm onboarding</span></li>
       <li><span><strong>Manage user access assignment: </strong>Assign use=
r access rights on product features easily in order to simplify feature onb=
oarding</span></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h3 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-FeatureGoals">Feature Goals</h3>
    <p><span>Agility and comprehensiveness of the configurations are import=
ant to this feature. The feature goals are:&nbsp;</span></p>
    <ul>
     <li>Expand the control structure of the firm &amp; user access config&=
nbsp;=20
      <ul>
       <li>As discussed in the gap analysis, it is not possible to generali=
ze the user roles of all NBIN firms and fit every user in a preset user gro=
up. The Product team would like to enable the associations between a user a=
nd the user access rights on all product features their firms have signed u=
p to. It is easier to understand what a user can/cannot access a specific f=
eature, rather than the pseudo "user group" they should function as. Beside=
s, the control structure is more scalable in case new features are added.</=
li>
       <li>The Product team would like to have a choice to customize the us=
er access rights across a firm or for a particular user on a specific produ=
ct feature, and apply suitable configuration.</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <ul>
     <li>Expand feature package configuration to the appropriate granular l=
evel and specification</li>
    </ul>
    <ul>
     <li style=3D"list-style-type: none;">
      <ul>
       <li>Feature access assignment should be able to trace the product fe=
ature hierarchy to include features under different product capabilities.</=
li>
       <li>Feature versioning should be available so that the Product team =
can set up a new digital package for a product of a newer version for the s=
ake of their rollout plan.</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h4 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Productfeaturehierarchy"><span style=
=3D"letter-spacing: -0.003em;">Product feature hierarchy</span></h4>
    <h5 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Overview"><span style=3D"letter-spaci=
ng: -0.003em;">Overview</span></h5>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-=
manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" h=
eight=3D"241" src=3D"ee75f7272a12480875be0c811d4235efc3db43f00a7befbc263cdd=
92e3f3caeb" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1393941690/image-2023-3=
-17_16-36-47.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1679085407233&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"14554=
11436" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"atta=
chment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2023-3-17_16-36-47.png"=
 data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D=
"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1393941690" data-linked-re=
source-container-version=3D"48" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></spa=
n></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p>When a firm has been assigned the access to a product feature, which=
 is the lowest level in the above product feature hierarchy, the firm featu=
re access right should be in effect in:&nbsp;</p>
    <ul>
     <li>Platform UI: Based on their firm-specific configuration, if any, p=
ermitted users of the firm will be able to see and access components and re=
sources related to that product feature if their user configuration is set =
up accordingly.</li>
     <li>Business APIs: They will have permission to call the endpoints in =
the specific APIs. <strong>Exception: Some APIs have specific constraints a=
nd won't be exposed to clients for direct access but via Platform UI only.<=
/strong></li>
     <li>Outside API calls: Cover the exception mentioned above. The permis=
sion should be inspected carefully by the contract of the firm and NBIN.</l=
i>
    </ul>
    <p>NOTE: The access permission should be granted on white-listing basis=
.</p>
    <p><br></p>
    <h5 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Inventoriesoffeaturesbyproduct-Extern=
alusersonly">Inventories of features by product - External users only</h5>
    <p>The following tables illustrate the product feature hierarchy by pro=
duct. Note that here it concerns with the levels where access control could=
 be applied, and it's not meant to represent the complete workflow.&nbsp;</=
p>
    <ul>
     <li>The tables are simplified to depict 1.0 features available to exte=
rnal users only; features which are only eligible to internal users are not=
 listed</li>
     <li>The "Feature Variation" column is not a separate level but is used=
 to describe the configurable options for the specified feature, if any</li=
>
     <li>In Orders (Trading), Equities trading product is not in-scoped for=
 1.0 but is depicted for illustration purpose</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Source: <a href=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca/display/NWPI/Feature+bundling=
+and+assignments+for+1.0" rel=3D"nofollow">Feature bundling and assignments=
 for 1.0 - NBIN - Web Platform and IAM - Confluence (bnc.ca)</a></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <div class=3D"rwui_tabs">
     <ul class=3D"rwui_tabs_menu">
      <!-- These will be generated by the js -->
     </ul><!-- Here will the tabs go -->
     <div class=3D"rwui_tab_content" data-name=3D"Orders" data-hash=3D"tab-=
Orders">
      <p class=3D"auto-cursor-target">The complete inventory of features fo=
r Orders is available at: <a href=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca/display/NWPI/Acces=
s+Control%3A+Orders" rel=3D"nofollow">Access Control: Orders - NBIN - Web P=
latform and IAM - Confluence (bnc.ca)</a></p>
      <div class=3D"table-wrap">
       <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
        <colgroup>
