 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h4 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Firmfeaturepackages-forfeatureaccessa=
ssignmenttofirms"><span>Firm feature packages - for feature access assignme=
nt to firms</span></h4>
    <h5 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Overview.1"><span>Overview</span></h5=
>
    <ul>
     <li>Firm feature package is composed of features (and other resources,=
 in the future) and available "feature variations" for firms to be assigned=
 to</li>
     <li>It is the atomic unit to assign feature access to firms; in other =
words, the Product team is not intended to offer firms the capability to ch=
oose individual features for onboarding, except for the <strong><em>add-on =
packages </em></strong>available alongside the firm feature packages=20
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Caution :warning:: The Product te=
am is not intended to create each and every feature (or feature group) as a=
n add-on and then conjugate them into various feature packages. The thought=
 process is to craft the basic packages according to our firms' needs based=
 on their firm type, as of 1.0 GA. There are several merits of offering a '=
feature package' as opposed to a mix of add-on packages:&nbsp;</span>
        <ul>
         <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">For Product team: Easier to man=
age expectation, lead firms into the vision/opportunities what Compass can =
offer for them, and strategize rollout plan &amp; marketing aspiraion</span=
></li>
         <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">For prospect firms: Simplifying=
 the offer, standardizing the cost, and accelerating the firm onboarding pr=
ocess&nbsp;</span></li>
         <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">For onboarded firms: Standardiz=
ing &amp; simplifying access control for the sake of inquiry &amp; trouble-=
shooting</span></li>
        </ul></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Having said that, the point of vi=
ew does not dictate the technical implementation</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">In addition, post-1.0, The Produc=
t team want to offer a <strong>self-serve customization capabilities for fi=
rms to manage UI visibility of features for their users across firm (i.e. a=
pply to all users) or per specific users.&nbsp;</strong></span>
        <ul>
         <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Case 1: Firm customization</spa=
n>
          <ul>
           <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Across the firm, <em>turn off=
 certain </em>feature(s) so that their users cannot see &amp; access these =
features via the Platform; however, the firm and their users still have the=
 access right to those features. The firm can turn on the feature(s) again =
to resume access via the Platform. </span></li>
           <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Business use case: The firm h=
as a similar feature offered to their users via another platform, and they =
are not ready to switch over to the CX features yet, though its access is i=
ncluded in the feature package they signed up for. When they are ready to s=
witch, they can turn on the feature across firm so that all accessible user=
s will be able to use it via the Platform. </span></li>
           <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Direct API calls: There is no=
 security concern if the firm make direct API calls to respective NBIN busi=
ness APIs because the access is included in their feature package.</span></=
li>
          </ul></li>
         <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Case 2: User customization</spa=
n>
          <ul>
           <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">The firm <em>turn off </em>ce=
rtain feature(s) for particular user(s) so that they cannot see &amp; acces=
s these features via the Platform though the feature(s) are included in the=
 user feature packages they are assigned to</span></li>
           <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Business use case: The firm w=
ant to control the use of certain features, e.g. those are softward licence=
 controlled or workflow dependent, ensuring that the usage is as expected a=
nd not being abused. They want to have the ability to turn it on/off among =
their users freely.&nbsp;</span></li>
           <li><span style=3D"color:#c9372c;">Direct API calls: Same as abo=
ve.</span></li>
          </ul></li>
        </ul></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li>Under applicable features, "feature variations" can be specified p=
er firm</li>
     <li>For more details, please refer to <a href=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca/d=
isplay/NWPI/Firm+Feature+Packages" rel=3D"nofollow">Firm Feature Packages -=
 NBIN - Web Platform and IAM - Confluence (bnc.ca)</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Below is a graphical interpre=
tation from Product perspective. </span><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0p=
x;">Caution </span>:warning:<span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">: It ser=
ves as an example for communication only.</span></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-=
manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" h=
eight=3D"179" src=3D"b95e7fbed87bcb6ad0de82bb037afec9de445c1629bc579291b5f0=
48ead5a31a" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1393941690/image-2023-3=
-18_17-31-23.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1679175083333&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"14554=
11920" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"atta=
chment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2023-3-18_17-31-23.png"=
 data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D=
"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1393941690" data-linked-re=
source-container-version=3D"48" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></spa=
n></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <h5 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Externalfirmfeaturepackagesfor1.0"><s=
pan style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">External firm feature packages for 1.0=
</span></h5>
    <p>The following tables illustrate the firm feature packages available =
to external firms. Only 1.0 features are depicted in the packages.</p>
    <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Caution </span>:warning:<span=
 style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">:</span></p>
    <ul>
     <li><strong>The lists of features are not finalized yet</strong></li>
     <li><strong>R2 functionalities and external applications offered in th=
e feature packages (see Source) are not listed in the tables and they will =
not be access controlled by CX yet - out-of 1.0 scope</strong>
      <ul>
       <li>
        <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">In 1.0, user access on ot=
her platforms (e.g. R2, SZ, Inform) cannot be controlled via CX; the access=
 control will be handled via the separate user profiles. </span></p></li>
       <li>
        <p><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">In post-1.0, F&amp;UM wil=
l attempt the 'unified user access' goal which means we can control SZ acce=
ss mappings and R2 access mappings via CX user management</span></p><strong=
><strong><span><span class=3D"ui-provider xk b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p =
q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak"> </span></span></strong></s=
trong>
        <p><br></p></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Source: <a href=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca/display/NWPI/Feature+bundling=
+and+assignments+for+1.0" rel=3D"nofollow">Feature bundling and assignments=
 for 1.0 - NBIN - Web Platform and IAM - Confluence (bnc.ca)</a></p>
    <p><br></p>
