 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h4 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Userfeaturepackages-forfeatureaccessa=
ssignmenttousers"><span>User feature packages - for feature access assignme=
nt to users</span></h4>
    <h5 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Overview.2">Overview</h5>
    <ul>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Similar to the concept of firm feat=
ure packages, the Product team wants to create "feature packages" assignabl=
e to any given group of users</span></li>
     <li>A "user grouping" is a group of users who have dedicated roles and=
 duties, and hence feature access needs, across all product lines and unive=
rsally among our client firms</li>
     <li>"Users feature package" is composed of features (and other resourc=
es, in the future) and available "feature variations" for groups of users t=
o be assigned to</li>
     <li>It is the atomic unit to assign feature access to users; in other =
words, the Product team is not intended to offer users the capability to ch=
oose individual features for onboarding, except for the <strong style=3D"le=
tter-spacing: 0.0px;"><em>user functions individually assigned per user, </=
em></strong><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">which provides user acce=
ss rights to additional features. For instance,</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"><strong>Security Stewards=
:</strong> They can perform use management activities for the range of user=
s they are allowed to manage</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"><strong>PM Sub-advisors:<=
/strong> They can perform trading capabilities on their <strong><em>sub-adv=
ising RR code ranges</em></strong> (specifically assigned per user)</span><=
/li>
      </ul></li>
     <li>Under applicable features, "feature variations" can be specified p=
er user</li>
     <li>There are two sets of user feature packages, one for External user=
s and one for Internal users. Details are listed in <a href=3D"https://wiki=
.bnc.ca/display/NWPI/Firm+Feature+Packages" rel=3D"nofollow" style=3D"lette=
r-spacing: 0.0px;">Firm Feature Packages - NBIN - Web Platform and IAM - Co=
nfluence (bnc.ca)</a><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;"> </span><span s=
tyle=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Caution </span>:warning:<span style=3D"lett=
er-spacing: 0.0px;">: It is work in progress.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><span>Below is a graphical interpretation from Product perspective. =
</span><span>Caution </span>:warning:<span>: It serves as an example for co=
mmunication only.</span></p>
    <p>Setup 1:&nbsp;</p>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-=
manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" h=
eight=3D"172" src=3D"a1da446ab0d987bb00abab9c8f2f6bc30ae9aa40ff110ca7b44808=
a882d905bd" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1393941690/image-2023-3=
-18_23-14-58.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1679195698577&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"14554=
11949" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"atta=
chment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2023-3-18_23-14-58.png"=
 data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D=
"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1393941690" data-linked-re=
source-container-version=3D"48" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></spa=
n></p>
    <p>Alternative setup:</p>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-=
manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" h=
eight=3D"202" src=3D"cb2aece5ebebe50e1b3a285e31af6c52be41103a7fc26acc660287=
e579be29ed" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1393941690/image-2023-3=
-20_10-59-50.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1679324390403&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"14554=
13964" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"atta=
chment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2023-3-20_10-59-50.png"=
 data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D=
"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1393941690" data-linked-re=
source-container-version=3D"48" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></spa=
n></p>
    <p><br></p>
    <h5 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Businessentityrelationdiagram">Busine=
ss entity relation diagram&nbsp;</h5>
    <ul>
     <li>This is a UML diagram depicting the business entities and their re=
lations so far discussed</li>
     <li><strong>Caution :warning:: It is by no means to be interpreted as =
any technical diagram or data schema</strong></li>
     <li><span>Summary of business entity relations:</span>
      <ul>
       <li><span>Any FEATURE PACKAGE is composed of FEATURE or FEATURES</sp=
an></li>
       <li><span>FIRM is assigned to one and only one FIRM FEATURE PACKAGE<=
/span></li>
       <li><span>FIRM is assigned to zero, one or many ADD-ON FEATURE PACKA=
GE(S)</span></li>
       <li><span>USER is belonged to one and only one USER GROUPING</span><=
/li>
       <li><span>USER FEATURE PACKAGE ASSIGNMENT is assigned to one and onl=
y one USER FEATURE PACKAGE and likewise</span></li>
       <li><span>USER FEATURE PACKAGE ASSIGNMENT is assigned to zero, one o=
r many USER FUNCTIONS PER USER</span></li>
       <li><span>FIRM is configured to zero, one or many FEATURE CONFIGURAT=
ION BY FIRM</span></li>
       <li><span>USER is configured to zero, one or many FEATURE CONFIGURAT=
ION BY USER</span></li>
       <li><span>FEATURE has CONFIGURATION and ACCESS RIGHT</span></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper confluence-embedded-=
manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" h=
eight=3D"277" src=3D"38b8bbf3261a82b707da97ef541809321441b71099da4b9f5a1e75=
23a72ce5c4" data-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1393941690/image-2023-3=
-20_14-56-33.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1679338593534&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"14554=
15267" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"atta=
chment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2023-3-20_14-56-33.png"=
 data-base-url=3D"https://wiki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D=
"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1393941690" data-linked-re=
source-container-version=3D"48" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468"></spa=
n></p>
    <p>.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h4 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-SettingandresolvingConfigurationandAc=
cesscontrol"><span style=3D"font-weight: 600;letter-spacing: -0.003em;">Set=
ting and resolving Configuration and Access control&nbsp;</span></h4>
    <h5 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Grantingfirm&amp;useraccess-Step-by-s=
tepexplanation">Granting firm &amp; user access - Step-by-step explanation<=
/h5>
    <ul>
     <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">Step 1: Set up firm and users</span=
>
      <ul>
       <li>This step is sometimes referred as firm &amp; user onboarding. A=
ssume that NBIN team has set up the firm profile and user profiles, then th=
ey will continue to set up the respective access assignments:</li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">For firm: Assign firm feature pac=
kage =E2=86=92 Assign add-on features =E2=86=92 Specify applicable feature =
configuration by firm&nbsp;</span></li>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">For users: Assign the suitable us=
er feature package to a user =E2=86=92 Assign additional user functions per=
 user =E2=86=92 Specify applicable feature configuration by user - the opti=
ons are bounded by the configurations selected by their firm</span></li>
      </ul></li>
     <li>Step 2: User attempts to gain access (via Platform or direct API c=
alls)=20
      <ul>
       <li><span style=3D"color:#172b4d;">In a nutshell, the features a giv=
en user has access to are the <strong><em>intersection (subset) </em></stro=
ng>of their firm's feature access and their user feature access</span></li>
       <li>The reasonings are:&nbsp;=20
        <ul>
         <li>Inheritance of controls / configs - from the FIRM hierarchy pe=
rspective&nbsp;=20
          <ul>
           <li class=3D"ql-indent-1">If a firm has access, their users have=
 the chance to have the ability to access, depending on the user profile se=
ttings. Conversely, if the firm does NOT have access, their users will NOT =
have a choice.</li>
           <li class=3D"ql-indent-1">User access is further refined by assi=
gnment of features to users via their user feature package assignment</li>
          </ul></li>
         <li>Control levels inherited from features above - from the FEATUR=
E hierarchy perspective=20
          <ul>
           <li class=3D"ql-indent-1">For instance, if a user has the abilit=
y to create requests, they can also view requests&nbsp;</li>
           <li class=3D"ql-indent-1">This is handled implicitly in the crea=
tion of user feature packages</li>
          </ul></li>
        </ul></li>
       <li>When "feature variations" are applicable to a feature, the assig=
ned feature variation(s) by the user should be applied to inform the resour=
ce / access control=20
        <ul>
         <li>For instance, the Book Order feature has available feature var=
iations, being Mutual Funds and Equities; a user has access to Book Order f=
eature must be specified which trading products, or both, they have access =
to</li>
         <li>Caution :warning:: Feature Variation is not equivalent to Acce=
ss Control, which implies the permission of use. "Feature Variation" can be=
 applied to enhance UI visibility or usability policies.</li>
        </ul></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <h5 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Specialbusinessusecases">Special busi=
ness use cases</h5>
    <p>There are basically two use cases of changes after a firm and their =
users are assigned to their respective firm feature package and user featur=
e packages:&nbsp;</p>
    <ol>
     <li><u><strong>Change firm feature access: </strong></u>The firm now w=
ants to add/remove their access to specific features, e.g. they have sold o=
ut certain business and don't need access to that area or they have signed =
up the service with another provider. In that case, they need to be assigne=
d to a NEW firm feature package. It's a<em> rare situation</em> as it is ca=
used by a change in the client's business model; when it happens, NBIN will=
 handle it as a special project. We will have to create a new firm feature =
package, move their users to the right user feature package or create new o=
nes if there is none suitable. <strong>F&amp;UM perspective: Deem this use =
case as out-of-scope. The access control implementation shall NOT allow any=
 change to an assigned firm feature package and the implication to their us=
er access assignments. In other words, a firm feature package is sealed onc=
e it's been assigned to a firm.</strong></li>
     <li><span><span class=3D"ui-provider gp b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p =
q r s t u v w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak"><u><strong>Customize firm /=
 user feature variation: </strong></u>The firm has access to a feature but =
they don't want all or some of their users to access it via the Platform UI=
, e.g. they have developed their own tool on their portal but want to use t=
he NBIN APIs to complete the job, or they want to hide the feature temporar=
ily and show it for their users to use later due to their training or roll-=
out schedule; on user-level, a firm may want to hide a critical feature fro=
m a new employee temporarily until their training is completed. This is the=
 <strong>"UI visibility" not the "access control" </strong>deviation. The f=
irm and eligible users still have the access to the feature, but if it's hi=
dden by configuration, they won't be able to access it via the Platform UI.=
 The show/hide feature is the post 1.0 self-serve firm feature, i.e. giving=
 firm administrators the ability to manage feature variations. <strong>F&am=
p;UM perspective: It doesn't pose any security concern because the firm and=
 their users have been rightfully assigned the access. If the firm wants to=
 restrict/strip user access, they will have to assign them to a different u=
ser feature package. That said, feature variation assignment doesn't impact=
 access control or trigger changes to their users' user group. The show/hid=
e characteristic by feature variation shall be implemented in the specific =
product line on the Platform, where it's relevant.</strong></span></span></=
li>
    </ol>
    <p><br></p>
    <div role=3D"region" aria-label=3D"Info" class=3D"confluence-informatio=
n-macro  confluence-information-macro-information">
     <span role=3D"presentation" class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconf=
ont-info-filled confluence-information-macro-icon"></span>
     <div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
      <p><u>Important Principle:</u> The Product team won't just fulfill th=
e customization wish of any firm causally. We've done our research to craft=
 out the proposed "user feature packages", which will accommodate the needs=
 of the majority of our firms &amp; users. Some user feature packages are n=
ot segregated by application (or bcm) but rather by access level, e.g. read=
 only, read &amp; write. For instance, for someone who has the <strong>View=
 all</strong> capability, they will have access to view orders/servicing re=
quests/account profiles/acct opening application; if their firm doesn't hav=
e access to one of the applications, there's no concern of abused access co=
ntrol because:&nbsp;</p>
      <ol>
       <li>There is <strong>no data </strong>of the firm in the missing app=
lication (or bcm). Thus, there is no concern of giving the 'scopes' to a us=
er who potentially can <em>view trading orders</em>, as an example, while t=
heir firm doesn't sign up to Compass trading as there is no trading data of=
 the firm.</li>
       <li>'Scopes' will have to be resolved into 'permission' for a legal =
API call. As the permission rules are governed by the NBIN Authorization AP=
I, which must check the access right of the firm first, and then grant acce=
ss to their users accordingly based on the step-by-step explanation above, =
user token which has the 'scopes' but not getting the right firm access ass=
ignment won't be granted the 'permission'.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>This is how the Product team have attempted to avoid creating too =
many user feature packages, and yet have the certainty that no illegal acce=
ss assignment is possible.&nbsp;</p>
     </div>
    </div>
    <p class=3D"auto-cursor-target">.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h3 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-KeyDeliverables">Key Deliverables</h3=
>
    <ul>
     <li><span style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Identify all firm types, at=
tributes &amp; hierarchies, and revise CX firm structure</span></li>
     <li><span>Understand the product feature hierarchy and level of contro=
ls required</span></li>
     <li><span>Enrich the provision of firm access on features</span></li>
     <li><span>Consider the customize-able access options, firm-wide and us=
er-level, for future versions</span></li>
     <li><span>Enable feature bundling config to the required granular leve=
l, specification and product version</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h3 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-SuccessMeasurement"><span style=3D"le=
tter-spacing: -0.006em;">Success Measurement</span></h3>
    <ul>
     <li><span style=3D"letter-spacing: -0.006em;">User access assignments =
are more intuitive, containing less "loaded" information as in a pseudo "us=
er group" which a user may or may not function as</span></li>
     <li>Digital packages (or feature bundles) are more agile and capable o=
f catering more granular level of the product feature hierarchy</li>
     <li>There is a room to apply customization in user access control acro=
ss firm or by user</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h3 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-BenefitHypothesis">Benefit Hypothesis=
</h3>
    <ul>
     <li>Accelerate the onboarding of new product features</li>
     <li>Accelerate the onboarding of new firms and users</li>
     <li>Contribute to NBIN's NPS</li>
     <li>Drive Compass-X adoption</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h3 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-ChangeManagement">Change Management</=
h3>
    <p>As the user access control solution has been implemented in producti=
on and there are several dozens of users participating in the beta runs of =
launched applications, change management is required to ensure there is no =
impact to the live activities. Besides, <span>documentations &amp; Knowledg=
e Base articles should be updated accordingly.</span></p>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h3 id=3D"Optimizelevelofcontrols-Exclusion">Exclusion</h3>
    <ul>
     <li>This feature does not cover Manage firm config capability and Mana=
ge user profile capability</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
